1
00:00:11,250 --> 00:00:12,293
August 5th,

2
00:00:12,293 --> 00:00:12,840
2010

3
00:00:12,840 --> 00:00:15,360
Deep under the Atacama Desert in Chile,

4
00:00:15,360 --> 00:00:17,960
a mountain of rock collapses inside a mine

5
00:00:18,330 --> 00:00:19,720
Thirty-three men are trapped,

6
00:00:19,720 --> 00:00:22,125
seven hundred metres below the surface

7
00:00:22,275 --> 00:00:23,985
They have food for only a couple of days

8
00:00:23,985 --> 00:00:26,557
And nobody knows if they are still alive

9
00:00:26,707 --> 00:00:29,132
They will spend sixty-nine days underground

10
00:00:29,282 --> 00:00:31,682
This is how they survived

11
00:00:34,550 --> 00:00:36,740
The San José mine was an old copper and

12
00:00:36,740 --> 00:00:38,838
gold mine in one of the driest deserts on

13
00:00:38,838 --> 00:00:39,707
Earth

14
00:00:39,857 --> 00:00:41,087
To reach the deepest tunnels,

15
00:00:41,087 --> 00:00:43,567
trucks drove down a long spiral road cut into

16
00:00:43,567 --> 00:00:44,676
the rock

17
00:00:44,826 --> 00:00:46,536
The mine had a bad safety record,

18
00:00:46,536 --> 00:00:48,230
but the pay was good

19
00:00:48,380 --> 00:00:50,090
On the afternoon of August 5th,

20
00:00:50,090 --> 00:00:52,294
the men felt the mountain shake

21
00:00:52,444 --> 00:00:54,834
Then a gigantic block of rock crashed down and

22
00:00:54,834 --> 00:00:57,234
sealed the only road out

23
00:01:00,583 --> 00:01:02,133
The dust was so thick the men could not

24
00:01:02,133 --> 00:01:03,824
see their own hands

25
00:01:03,974 --> 00:01:04,564
When it cleared,

26
00:01:04,564 --> 00:01:06,604
they found the way out was blocked by solid

27
00:01:06,604 --> 00:01:07,586
rock

28
00:01:07,736 --> 00:01:09,926
They gathered in a small emergency shelter,

29
00:01:09,926 --> 00:01:12,416
about the size of a small apartment

30
00:01:12,566 --> 00:01:13,076
It was hot,

31
00:01:13,076 --> 00:01:14,916
around thirty degrees Celsius,

32
00:01:14,916 --> 00:01:16,527
and very humid

33
00:01:16,677 --> 00:01:18,907
The shelter held emergency food meant to last

34
00:01:18,907 --> 00:01:21,307
only a couple of days

35
00:01:24,450 --> 00:01:27,050
The shift foreman took charge and made a plan

36
00:01:27,353 --> 00:01:29,223
Every man would eat the same tiny meal,

37
00:01:29,223 --> 00:01:31,163
once every two days

38
00:01:31,313 --> 00:01:32,623
Two spoonfuls of tuna,

39
00:01:32,623 --> 00:01:35,203
a sip of milk and a bite of cracker

40
00:01:35,353 --> 00:01:35,863
For water,

41
00:01:35,863 --> 00:01:37,823
they drank from tanks meant for cooling the

42
00:01:37,823 --> 00:01:38,943
machines

43
00:01:39,232 --> 00:01:39,982
On average,

44
00:01:39,982 --> 00:01:41,862
each man lost about eight kilograms

45
00:01:41,862 --> 00:01:43,942
But they stayed together

46
00:01:47,583 --> 00:01:48,253
On the surface,

47
00:01:48,253 --> 00:01:50,293
families rushed to the mine and refused to

48
00:01:50,293 --> 00:01:51,276
leave

49
00:01:51,426 --> 00:01:54,026
Their tents became a village called Camp Hope

50
00:01:54,318 --> 00:01:56,388
Rescuers began drilling narrow holes into the

51
00:01:56,388 --> 00:01:56,828
mountain,

52
00:01:56,828 --> 00:01:58,828
trying to hit the tunnels where the men might

53
00:01:58,828 --> 00:01:59,718
be

54
00:01:59,868 --> 00:02:01,098
But the maps of the mine were old,

55
00:02:01,098 --> 00:02:03,120
and the drills kept missing

56
00:02:03,270 --> 00:02:03,860
Days passed

57
00:02:03,860 --> 00:02:06,460
Many feared the miners were dead

58
00:02:09,717 --> 00:02:10,707
On day seventeen,

59
00:02:10,707 --> 00:02:13,147
a drill broke through into a tunnel,

60
00:02:13,147 --> 00:02:14,907
688 metres down

61
00:02:15,499 --> 00:02:16,409
The men heard it coming

62
00:02:16,409 --> 00:02:18,289
They tied notes to the drill and hammered on

63
00:02:18,289 --> 00:02:19,425
the steel

64
00:02:19,575 --> 00:02:20,845
When rescuers pulled it up,

65
00:02:20,845 --> 00:02:23,445
they found a message written in red ink

66
00:02:23,604 --> 00:02:25,745
'Estamos bien en el refugio,

67
00:02:25,745 --> 00:02:28,434
los 33.' We are well in the shelter,

68
00:02:28,434 --> 00:02:29,874
the 33

69
00:02:30,176 --> 00:02:32,776
All of Chile erupted in celebration

70
00:02:36,350 --> 00:02:38,300
Now rescuers could send supplies down the

71
00:02:38,300 --> 00:02:39,637
narrow hole

72
00:02:39,787 --> 00:02:41,817
They used thin tubes called palomas,

73
00:02:41,817 --> 00:02:43,457
which means doves

74
00:02:43,607 --> 00:02:44,677
Down came water,

75
00:02:44,677 --> 00:02:45,197
food,

76
00:02:45,197 --> 00:02:45,917
medicine,

77
00:02:45,917 --> 00:02:47,777
and letters from home

78
00:02:47,927 --> 00:02:49,877
Soon the men could even see and talk to

79
00:02:49,877 --> 00:02:51,806
their families through a cable

80
00:02:51,956 --> 00:02:53,586
But the hole was far too narrow for a

81
00:02:53,586 --> 00:02:53,906
person

82
00:02:53,906 --> 00:02:56,506
Getting them out would be much harder

83
00:02:59,650 --> 00:03:01,680
Experts warned that a rescue could take until

84
00:03:01,680 --> 00:03:02,800
Christmas

85
00:03:02,994 --> 00:03:05,304
So Chile tried three giant drills at the same

86
00:03:05,304 --> 00:03:05,664
time:

87
00:03:05,664 --> 00:03:06,424
Plan A,

88
00:03:06,424 --> 00:03:08,661
Plan B and Plan C

89
00:03:08,811 --> 00:03:11,321
Plan B used a powerful drill normally used for

90
00:03:11,321 --> 00:03:12,041
water wells,

91
00:03:12,041 --> 00:03:14,641
to widen one of the existing holes

92
00:03:14,930 --> 00:03:16,560
Experts from around the world helped,

93
00:03:16,560 --> 00:03:19,160
including doctors and engineers from NASA

94
00:03:19,946 --> 00:03:21,096
It was a race against time,

95
00:03:21,096 --> 00:03:23,176
and against the rock

96
00:03:26,450 --> 00:03:27,000
Underground,

97
00:03:27,000 --> 00:03:29,600
the men organised their days like a small town

98
00:03:30,166 --> 00:03:30,836
They had jobs,

99
00:03:30,836 --> 00:03:31,916
shifts for sleeping,

100
00:03:31,916 --> 00:03:34,509
and lights to mark day and night

101
00:03:34,659 --> 00:03:35,449
They exercised,

102
00:03:35,449 --> 00:03:36,289
prayed together,

103
00:03:36,289 --> 00:03:38,689
and voted on important decisions

104
00:03:39,060 --> 00:03:40,930
Doctors on the surface checked on their health

105
00:03:40,930 --> 00:03:42,127
every day

106
00:03:42,277 --> 00:03:44,467
Staying calm and staying united kept them

107
00:03:44,467 --> 00:03:45,587
alive

108
00:03:49,117 --> 00:03:49,987
On October 9th,

109
00:03:49,987 --> 00:03:51,547
at 8:05 in the morning,

110
00:03:51,547 --> 00:03:53,960
the Plan B drill broke through

111
00:03:54,110 --> 00:03:54,860
Above ground,

112
00:03:54,860 --> 00:03:55,980
families cheered,

113
00:03:55,980 --> 00:03:57,676
hugged and cried

114
00:03:57,826 --> 00:03:59,976
The new shaft was more than six hundred metres

115
00:03:59,976 --> 00:04:00,216
long,

116
00:04:00,216 --> 00:04:02,816
and only about seventy centimetres wide

117
00:04:03,341 --> 00:04:05,571
Engineers lined the top of the shaft with steel

118
00:04:05,571 --> 00:04:07,917
pipe to keep it from collapsing

119
00:04:08,067 --> 00:04:09,577
Now they needed a way to bring the men

120
00:04:09,577 --> 00:04:10,697
up

121
00:04:14,083 --> 00:04:16,615
The answer was a capsule named Phoenix

122
00:04:16,765 --> 00:04:18,475
It was built by the Chilean Navy,

123
00:04:18,475 --> 00:04:20,436
with advice from NASA

124
00:04:20,586 --> 00:04:22,456
It was just fifty-four centimetres wide,

125
00:04:22,456 --> 00:04:24,918
barely wider than a man's shoulders

126
00:04:25,068 --> 00:04:26,098
It carried oxygen,

127
00:04:26,098 --> 00:04:26,818
a radio,

128
00:04:26,818 --> 00:04:29,418
and an escape hatch in case it got stuck

129
00:04:30,060 --> 00:04:31,610
Each miner would ride it alone,

130
00:04:31,610 --> 00:04:34,210
more than six hundred metres straight up

131
00:04:37,683 --> 00:04:39,033
Late on October 12th,

132
00:04:39,033 --> 00:04:41,393
the first rescuer rode the capsule down into

133
00:04:41,393 --> 00:04:42,526
the mine

134
00:04:42,676 --> 00:04:43,666
Just after midnight,

135
00:04:43,666 --> 00:04:45,346
the first miner reached the surface,

136
00:04:45,346 --> 00:04:47,641
and the crowd exploded with joy

137
00:04:47,791 --> 00:04:49,791
Millions of people around the world watched it

138
00:04:49,791 --> 00:04:50,730
live

139
00:04:50,880 --> 00:04:51,510
One by one,

140
00:04:51,510 --> 00:04:52,750
about every forty minutes,

141
00:04:52,750 --> 00:04:53,670
the men came up,

142
00:04:53,670 --> 00:04:56,270
wearing dark glasses to protect their eyes

143
00:04:56,744 --> 00:04:58,574
The last miner up was the shift foreman,

144
00:04:58,574 --> 00:05:01,174
who had led them from the very first day

145
00:05:04,650 --> 00:05:06,160
At 9:56 that night,

146
00:05:06,160 --> 00:05:08,200
the last miner stepped out of the capsule

147
00:05:08,200 --> 00:05:10,280
All 33 were alive

148
00:05:10,502 --> 00:05:12,532
Then the rescuers who had gone down came back

149
00:05:12,532 --> 00:05:13,754
up too

150
00:05:13,904 --> 00:05:15,774
The men had survived sixty-nine days

151
00:05:15,774 --> 00:05:16,334
underground,

152
00:05:16,334 --> 00:05:18,561
a record for trapped miners

153
00:05:18,711 --> 00:05:21,341
Chile hired more mine inspectors and tightened

154
00:05:21,341 --> 00:05:23,008
its safety rules

155
00:05:23,158 --> 00:05:25,628
And Los 33 became a symbol of hope around

156
00:05:25,628 --> 00:05:27,068
the world

157
00:05:27,617 --> 00:05:28,407
Thirty-three men

158
00:05:28,407 --> 00:05:30,367
Seven hundred metres of rock

159
00:05:30,367 --> 00:05:31,775
Sixty-nine days

160
00:05:31,925 --> 00:05:33,675
Could you have survived seventeen days on two

161
00:05:33,675 --> 00:05:35,143
spoonfuls of tuna?

162
00:05:35,293 --> 00:05:36,689
Tell me in the comments

163
00:05:36,839 --> 00:05:39,439
Subscribe so you don't miss the next episode
